#NEXUS
[Phylogram: synthetic substitutions per site; NOT time.
 Shared synthetic taxa: OTU01 through OTU15; shared strictly binary topology.
 Internal prob values are random synthetic probabilities above 0.85 (85%),
 for display testing only, NOT analysis results.
 Root child distances: 0.3 and 0.2.
 Tip distances: 0.4, 0.5, then 0.4 through 1.6 in steps of 0.1.]
BEGIN TREES;
  TREE phylogram = [&R]
    ((OTU01:0.1,OTU02:0.2)[&prob=0.953]:0.3,
     (((OTU03:0.18,OTU04:0.28)[&prob=0.992]:0.01,(OTU05:0.38,OTU06:0.48)[&prob=0.949]:0.01)[&prob=0.946]:0.01,
      (((OTU07:0.57,OTU08:0.67)[&prob=0.854]:0.01,(OTU09:0.77,OTU10:0.87)[&prob=0.955]:0.01)[&prob=0.899]:0.01,
       ((OTU11:0.97,OTU12:1.07)[&prob=0.898]:0.01,(OTU13:1.17,(OTU14:1.26,OTU15:1.36)[&prob=0.999]:0.01)[&prob=0.934]:0.01)[&prob=0.952]:0.01)[&prob=0.886]:0.01)[&prob=0.919]:0.2)
      [&branch_length_unit=substitutions_per_site,prob=0.856];
END;
